   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The model is \\( \\frac{dN}{dt} = kN \\). Separating and integrating gives \\( \\ln|N| = kt + C \\), so \\( N = N_0 e^{kt} \\), and the value at t = 0 gives \\( N_0 = 380 \\).",
         "rule_named": "separation of variables for proportional growth"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The second value gives \\( 190 = 380 e^{5k} \\), so \\( k = - \\frac{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{5} \\).",
         "rule_named": "constant from a second data pair"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Therefore \\( N(t) = 380 e^{- \\frac{t \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}{5}} \\) insects.",
